{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978173-making-the-ultimate-sword","id":978173,"title":"Making the Ultimate Sword","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-28T20:50:47-07:00","id":978173,"title":"Making the Ultimate Sword","content":"I'm wanting to make a mage who's main goal is to create a sword that will make him a name remembered through out history. He's obsessed with the ideal of perfecting himself and sees the symbol of a sword as a perfect quest to drive him to his peak. The process of forging the sword would also be a great work of forging himself.<br /> <br /> So I was hoping for some ideals on what type minor goals and quests and mysterys as lead ups to this ultimate work and what skills could he master to help him. Like I was thinking could there be some using the rules of making a soul stone to make like a super enhanced item like him making his soul stone out of an amagram of all perfected metals and using that to forge the blade or as an experiment ect... Cool and crazy ideals welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:01:18-07:00","id":978175,"title":"","content":"Seeking out rare metals with which to construct the perfect blade,<br /> Learning weapon forging techniques of ancient smithing masters to work the metal perfectly,<br /> Learning techniques for how to wield a blade because a blade is only as good as the one using it,<br /> Practicing ceremonies remembered no longer by mortals to infuse it with power,<br /> Maybe resisting that tantalizing deal the abyss is offering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:31:49-07:00","id":978186,"title":"","content":"For mastering skills - Crafts is an obvious one. I'd also nominate Science, to perfect his understanding of how metals behave under various kinds of stress, what his ultimate sword should look like at a fundamental level, etc.<br /> <br /> For quests:<br /> - Plenty of practice making and studying the various Perfected Materials seems like a must.<br /> - Seek out sword-based Artifacts and give them a thorough magical study, to see how Supernal power is bound into their material makeup. Other weapon artifacts would likely also be informative.<br /> - Seek out weapons that have had spirits bound into them (are Fetishes still a thing in Werewolf 2e? If so, they'd be perfect for this), and see how the presence of a spirit has changed them to bring them closer to the concept that the spirit represents. Make sure to seek out a variety of types of spirit, to see what difference it makes.<br /> - Examine various useful metals with Matter Sight and Matter Knowing/Unveiling spells as they undergo various stresses. What does steel look like as it's being heated? When it's molten? As it cools? How about aluminium? Titanium?<br /> - Seek out more exotic metals to give them the same study - what does metallic hydrogen look like under magical observation?<br /> - Consider how the properties of the various materials he's studied could contribute to his ideal sword, and how he can combine those properties from multiple materials.<br /> - Observe talented craftspeople at work - what happens to their auras as they create? How does the state of their minds and souls affect the finished product? How does the act of creation change them afterwards? How does the nature of what they're making affect that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:53:00-07:00","id":978201,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the idea that yantras are items that symbolize the nature and intent of the magic, you can apply that idea to your sword. For example if you decide to place a precious gem as decoration on the cross hilt or pommel don't just settle for a big rock, make it the stone from the ring of a Tectonic knight from the Crusades, then on the other side place a stone from the ring of one of Saladin's commanders. Make each element a symbol and accompanying quest of its own that fits the imbued and enhanced traits of the blade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:04:08-07:00","id":978204,"title":"","content":"Examining weapons of various sorts could help sort out which supernal symbols need to be represented in his work. Watching the interactions between warrior and weapon makes sense. Learning to wield a sword, as Yelesom said, is an obvious place to look.<br /> <br /> Alchemy, of course, might figure in. Perfecting the materials would be an obvious potential step. <br /> (As far as legacies go, both the Forgemasters and Uncrowned Kings fit beautifully.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Mysteries, eh? Lessee:<br /> <br /> Certain blades literally hum when wielded in combat by sufficiently skilled artists, but only by specific styles. Why is that?<br /> Drawing out the spirit of the weapon seems to be an art mortal martial artists can accomplish. Were they transforming into something inhuman? <br /> A Moros warrior awakens the blade he wields. He claims to never have studied Spirit.<br /> Certain materials and geometries make a blade transmit force and even magic. Does this require active skill on the part of the warrior or a blade that has a will of its own?<br /> Weapons and techniques can actually cast spells. These seem to draw on supernal magic without requiring a watchtower. The effects seem to bolster the soul of the wielder and make them resist magic. Some seem to enhance the mind and focus of the wielder.<br /> Why do some weapons break at inopportune times and others hold through to the last? Sure, you start with the superficial matter of force applied, but should move past this to the materials, fate, and will of all involved.<br /> Why *did* that chicken cross the road?<br /> The greatest swordsmith of all time was (pick an appropriate choice for the character. Japanese choices could be Masamune,, Muramasa, Yoshitsuni). How did he do it? Where did his first blade go? The last? How has the blade shaped destiny? Who held them over the years and how did they use them? Obsession about <i>any</i> aspect of a master's process would make sense early on in the character's career.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:36:43-07:00","id":978223,"title":"","content":"thanks guys i love this kinda of stuff.<br /> what about trying mythical and fantasy inspired forging techniques, like capturing a soul and some how using it to fuel the forge and quenching in the virgin blood of a maiden but at the same time using the ashes of saints in the metal mix and blessed silver by seven priest.<br /> Traveling into the Astral to find several fantasy swords to study and rip into the real word to melt down and use for materials.<br /> creating a death, spirit and mind ephemera copy of a physical sword and binding them all together.<br /> finding spirits or ghost skilled in forging and swords and some how studying under them<br /> traveling into the hedge underworld and shadow for impossible materials<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}